      "text": "Long-distance trade and credit instruments are older than money itself. The core financial technologies — interest-bearing loans, bills of exchange, partnership contracts — were invented not once but several times across disconnected civilizations. The medieval period ended not with barbarism but with the most sophisticated pre-modern commercial network in history."
